{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNUCkcwT1F542QirUSq9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #334 as `done` and wrote `.ard/334/triage-lead.md`. It sends the issue only to `triage:engineer`, and worker `engineer` will implement it.\n\n**The finding:** the cve scanner reported a high-severity flaw in `pymdown-extensions` 10.9.0, fixed in 11.0.1. Certain text in the docs' Markdown can make it hang (a ReDoS, a slow-regex denial of service). The package isn't listed in `docs/site/requirements.txt`. It comes in through the pinned `mkdocs-material` 9.5.50, and `mkdocs.yml` doesn't turn on any of its extensions directly.\n\n**Why only engineer:** the fix only touches the dependencies used to build the docs site. There's no new feature, user-facing change or public API involved, so product-manager, designer and documentation-planner aren't needed. Engineer is the only triage role that exists here besides lead.\n\n**For a maintainer to watch:**\n- **Major version jump:** the fixed release moves from 10.x to 11.x. The pinned `mkdocs-material` may not accept it, so it might need a bump too.\n- **No automatic docs check:** the configured tests (`make test`) only cover the Go code. Someone needs to check by hand that the docs site still builds.\n- **No design review:** there's no architect role in this repo, so nobody will review the major-version upgrade at that level. It only affects the docs build tools."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":766,"cache_read_input_tokens":11324,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":766},"output_tokens":481,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"215e00e2-fe68-4a79-b037-f54b0939f709","u